Build option MESEN_MAPPER_INPUT_READS: a read of a cartridge's own input
device is a read of the controls.

Karaoke Studio's cartridge (mapper 188) has a microphone with two buttons,
which the game reads at $6000-$7FFF through the mapper, not through the
controller ports. Mesen's lag counter and the host's input-read hook (patch
0003) saw only the controller ports, so a frame that read only the
microphone counted as a lag frame. With this option the mapper's read sets
the control manager's input-read flag, as a read of $4016 does. Off,
nothing changes.

--- a/Core/NES/Mappers/Bandai/BandaiKaraoke.h
+++ b/Core/NES/Mappers/Bandai/BandaiKaraoke.h
@@ -32,6 +32,12 @@
 
 	uint8_t ReadRegister(uint16_t addr) override
 	{
+#ifdef MESEN_MAPPER_INPUT_READS
+		//The microphone's buttons are read here, not through $4016/$4017:
+		//this read too is a read of the controls (no lag frame, and the
+		//host's hook is called)
+		_console->GetControlManager()->SetInputReadFlag();
+#endif
 		return _microphone->ReadRam(addr) | _console->GetMemoryManager()->GetOpenBus(0xF8);
 	}
 
